device.notes:
Xiaomi/Huami (now Zepp) bands and watches — Mi Band 2/3/4/5/6/7 and the Amazfit Bip/GTR/GTS/T-Rex family — speak BLE and can be driven locally with no cloud once an auth key is known. Gadgetbridge is the definitive documentation and implementation (the largest wearable-protocol RE project).
AUTH: older Mi Band 1/1S/2 pair with a client-chosen key. From ~Mi Band 4 / Amazfit Bip Lite onward the auth key is SERVER-generated — it must be extracted once from the official app (Mi Fit / Zepp), after which local control works offline. Unpairing in the official app invalidates the key.
GATT (Mi Band 2+): auth characteristic 00000009-0000-3512-2118-0009af100700 on the custom base 0000xxxx-0000-3512-2118-0009af100700. Three-step handshake on the auth characteristic:
  1. send key:      { 0x01, 0x08, <16-byte secret key> }
  2. request random:{ 0x02, 0x08 }
  3. send response: { 0x03, 0x08, <AES-ECB(random) with the key> }
Encryption is AES/ECB/NoPadding, 16-byte key; success responses are { 0x10, <command byte>, 0x01 }.
OLDER Mi Band 1/1S (service FEE0): device info FF01, name FF02, notification FF03, user info FF04, control point FF05, realtime steps FF06, activity data FF07, battery FF0C.
Per-generation characteristic maps beyond auth are best taken from Gadgetbridge source for the exact model.
